# THE PRELUDE: a fixpoint combinator and the Scott encoding.
#
# Everything here is pure lambda: no arithmetic, no constants. Scott rather
# than Church because the corpora match on data, and a Scott constructor IS
# its own case analysis: applied to its handlers, a cyclic list hands its
# head and its tail to the one that matches.
#
# A POINT IS AN EXPORTED UNARY PREDICATE, so this file is an ordinary Prolog
# module and another corpus reaches these pieces through `use_module`.
#
# EVERY BINDER IS A DISTINCT PROLOG VARIABLE within one clause, and a piece
# that is reused is pulled in by calling its predicate rather than repeated
# as text, which yields a fresh copy of the clause's variables every time.

#   The Y combinator. `fixpoint @ F` reduces to `F @ (fixpoint @ F)`.
λ export. export λx_0. (λx_1. x_0 λ. x_1 x_1) λx_1. x_0 λ. x_1 x_1
